# Code Hierarchy Rules

## File Organization

Both `a2a-client` and `a2a-server` are structured as monorepos with multiple packages. The `a2a-server` is currently undergoing migration from a monolithic `src/` structure to independent packages in the `packages/` directory.

### Migration Status

- **Source**: Files in `a2a-server/src/` are being migrated to `a2a-server/packages/`
- **Target**: Each package has clear responsibility boundaries and can be versioned independently
- **Feature Flags**: System supports granular enable/disable of features via configuration
- **Workspaces**: npm workspaces manage inter-package dependencies

### Package Responsibilities

| Package | Scope | Description |
|---------|-------|-------------|
| @a2a/server-config | Configuration | Environment variables, feature flags, validation |
| @a2a/server-utils | Utilities | Pure functions, logging, crypto, validation |
| @a2a/server-protocol | Types | Protocol definitions, interfaces, type guards |
| @a2a/server-core | Orchestration | Request processing, base processors, cognition |
| @a2a/server-transform | Pipeline | Transform operations, materialization |
| @a2a/server-llm | AI Services | LLM integration, cognition injection, reasoning |
| @a2a/server-p2p | Networking | P2P nodes, CRDT, peer discovery |
| @a2a/server-daemon | Background | Polling services, request processing daemons |
| @a2a/server-actions | Execution | Action registry, file/git/script operations |
| @a2a/server | Application | Main app, HTTP server, routes, middleware |

